{
  "description": "Retrieval ground truth for the portfolio chatbot. Each case is a question a recruiter, hiring manager, or technical interviewer might realistically ask. A retrieved chunk counts as relevant if its text contains ANY phrase in `relevant_phrases` (case-insensitive, whitespace-normalized). Matching on phrases rather than chunk IDs keeps the labels valid across re-chunking and re-indexing.",
  "splits": {
    "description": "Every case belongs to exactly one split. `dev` is where parameters, weights and stage choices are decided; `holdout` is never looked at while deciding one, so the published numbers are not the numbers something was tuned against. Assignment is deterministic rather than hand-picked — cases sorted by sha256(\"portfolio-golden-split-v1:\" + id), the first 40% held out — so it can be recomputed and audited, and so nobody can move an inconvenient question across the line. It is recorded here rather than computed at run time because a frozen split is the whole point: recomputing it would silently reshuffle every case the day an id is edited or a question is added.",
    "salt": "portfolio-golden-split-v1",
    "holdoutFraction": 0.4
  },
